# Line endings.
#
# Gradle's wrapper script is executed by /bin/sh. A CRLF `gradlew` fails on macOS and Linux with
# "bad interpreter: No such file or directory", which is the least informative message in the
# entire toolchain — and it happens the first time a Windows developer's commit is cloned by
# anyone else. Forcing LF on the text files, and marking the wrapper explicitly, removes it.
* text=auto eol=lf

gradlew text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary, so git never rewrites bytes inside them or tries to merge them.
*.jar binary
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary

